.TH POWERFUL-TOOLS 1 "September 2026" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
powerful-tools \- Powerful Tools desktop utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B powerful-tools
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIFILES\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the Powerful Tools window, or runs one tool directly. Only one
instance runs; further invocations are passed to it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-run
Open the Quick Launcher launcher.
.TP
.B \-\-pick\-color
Pick a color from the screen.
.TP
.B \-\-text\-extract
Select a screen area and copy its text (OCR).
.TP
.B \-\-ruler
Open the Screen Ruler.
.TP
.B \-\-always\-on\-top
Toggle always-on-top for the focused window (X11).
.TP
.B \-\-advanced\-paste
Open Advanced Paste.
.TP
.B \-\-shortcut\-guide
Open the Shortcut Guide.
.TP
.BR \-\-peek ", " \-\-rename ", " \-\-resize ", " \-\-unlocker " " \fIFILES\fR
Preview, bulk rename, resize or check locks of FILES.
.TP
.BI \-\-page " NAME"
Open a tool page, for example hosts or envvars.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
~/.config/powerful-tools/settings.json
